  "query_preview": "..\nA trough is expected to affect the southeast tonight and bring\nsome rain and snow showers. There is a decent chance this will\naccumulate less than one tenth of an inch of precipitation. Some\ngusty southeast winds are expected tomorrow.\n\nThe latest GFS ensemble shows a trough bringing more precipitation\non Tuesday into Wednesday. There is a better chance of receiving\nmore than one tenth of an inch of precipitation in this time\nperiod in the western half of the area, and lower chances in the\neast.\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS:\nNo deviations from the main forecast.\n\nThere is moderate confidence of precipitation amounts tonight and\nprecipitation on Monday night into Tuesday.",
